      "part_type": "Hadith",
      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:198:4",
      "text": [
        " مَنْ تَعَجَّلَ فِي يَوْمَيْنِ فَلَا يَنْفِرْ حَتَّى تَزُولَ الشَّمْسُ فَإِنْ أَدْرَكَهُ الْمَسَاءُ بَاتَ وَ لَمْ يَنْفِرْ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Muawiya Bin Ammar, and from Hammad, from al Halby, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> having said: ‘The one who hastens during the two days, so he should not depart until the sun (starts to) decline. So if he sees the evening, he should spend the night and not depart’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ibn abu ‘Umayr from Mu‘awiyah ibn ‘Ammar and Hammad from al-Halabiy who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘Whoever departs earlier in the second day he cannot do so before Zawal (declining of the sun toward the west at noontime), and if it becomes evening he must stay for the night, instead of departing.” "
        ]
      }
    },
